<title>USA: Continental to start two new Latam flights.</title>
<headline>Continental to start two new Latam flights.</headline>
<dateline>NEWARK, N.J. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines said on Friday it would begin daily non-stop service to Panama City, Panama and Guayaquil, Ecuador from N.J.'s Newark International Airport starting Sunday.</p>
<p>Continental said it was offering a special introductory fare of $99 one way between Newark and Panama and $119 one-way between Newark and Guayaquil. Passengers had to travel before December 15 and the last date to buy a ticket at these fares was November 15, it said.</p>
<p>The airline said the new flights were part of its plan to become the premiere U.S. airline serving Latin America from the New York area.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
